WEBVTT

00:01:27.649 --> 00:01:30.849
Now, this is a big question
that requires many studies.

00:01:31.269 --> 00:01:33.570
But the first step
to uncovering this question

00:01:33.594 --> 00:01:35.769
is to investigate when in development

00:01:35.793 --> 00:01:38.510
we become sensitive
to others' evaluations.

00:01:39.245 --> 00:01:42.125
I have spent the past four years
at Emory University

00:01:42.149 --> 00:01:44.236
investigating how an infant,

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:48.546
who has no problem walking
around the grocery store in her onesie,

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:51.421
develops into an adult
that fears public speaking

00:01:51.445 --> 00:01:53.546
for fear of being negatively judged.

00:01:54.472 --> 00:01:56.109
(Laughter)

00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:58.474
Now, this is usually a point
when people ask me,

00:01:58.498 --> 00:02:01.077
"How do you investigate
this question, exactly?